Negative `maxPresetColors` values produce incorrect behavior. `!(-5)` is `false` and `-5 === Infinity` is `false`, so the code falls through to `combined.slice(-(-5))` = `combined.slice(5)`, which silently *removes the first 5 items* instead of disabling the limit or clamping to zero. This contradicts the documented intent that only `0` and `Infinity` disable the limit. Fix by adding an explicit lower-bound guard:

```ts
if (maxPresetColors <= 0 || maxPresetColors === Infinity) {
  return combined;
}
```

This correctly handles 0, all negatives, and `Infinity` in one readable condition.
